# TPTP ATP Benchmark on Helma

This notebook runs a TPTP benchmark on the Helma HPC cluster and compares the following automated theorem provers:

- LEO-II
- Zipperposition
- E-Prover
- Vampire
- LEO-III
- ShotTx

The benchmark runner handles TPTP preparation, prover images, SLURM execution, result collection, and reporting.

---

## 1. Install the benchmark runner

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:atp_benchmark_runner,
   github: "penthooose/atp_benchmark_runner",
   force: true}
])
```

---

## 2. Configure the environment

```elixir
setup =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.prepare_livebook_setup(
    submit_label: "Setup"
  )

env_map = setup.env_map
env_file = setup.env_file
ssh_key_path = setup.ssh_key_path
```

---

## 3. Connect to Helma

```elixir
boot =
  HpcConnect.bootstrap(
    mode: :local,
    env_file: env_file,
    cluster: env_map["HPC_CONNECT_CLUSTER"] || "helma",
    username: env_map["HPC_CONNECT_USERNAME"],
    key_path: env_map["HPC_CONNECT_IDENTITY_FILE"]
  )

session = boot.session

IO.inspect(
  %{
    cluster: session.cluster.name,
    ssh_alias: session.ssh_alias,
    username: session.username,
    work_dir: session.work_dir,
    vault_dir: session.vault_dir
  },
  label: "Resolved HPC session"
)
```

---

## 4. Prepare TPTP and select provers

Download and extract the official TPTP archive if it is not already available.

```elixir
archive_result =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.ensure_tptp_archive()

IO.inspect(
  archive_result,
  label: "TPTP archive"
)
```

Load all problems from the installed TPTP library.

Axiom files are excluded because the benchmark operates on TPTP problems.

```elixir
problems =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.load_tptp_problems(
    include_axioms: false
  )

selected_provers = [
  :leo2,
  :zipperposition,
  :eprover,
  :vampire,
  :leo3,
  :shot_tx
]

available_provers =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.Provers.names()

missing_provers =
  selected_provers -- available_provers

if missing_provers != [] do
  raise "Unavailable provers: #{inspect(missing_provers)}"
end

summary =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.TPTP.summarize(problems)

IO.inspect(
  summary,
  label: "TPTP problem summary"
)

IO.puts("")
IO.puts("Problems: #{length(problems)}")
IO.puts("Provers: #{length(selected_provers)}")

IO.puts(
  "Prover/problem combinations: " <>
    "#{length(problems) * length(selected_provers)}"
)

IO.puts("")
IO.puts("Selected provers:")

Enum.each(selected_provers, fn prover ->
  IO.puts("  - #{prover}")
end)
```

---

## 5. Run the benchmark on Helma

The benchmark uses one Helma CPU node and executes prover tasks in parallel.

Missing Apptainer prover images are prepared automatically before execution.

```elixir
plan =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.bootstrap(
    session,
    selected_provers,
    problems,
    mode: :hpc,
    hpc_mode: :single_node,
    single_node_mode: :parallel,
    node_size: :half,
    max_parallel_jobs: 6,
    timeout_seconds: 30,
    prepare_images: true,
    extended_debug: false
  )

IO.puts("Run ID: #{plan.id}")
IO.puts("Problems: #{length(problems)}")
IO.puts("Provers: #{length(selected_provers)}")

IO.puts(
  "Prover/problem combinations: " <>
    "#{length(problems) * length(selected_provers)}"
)

results =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.run_benchmark(plan)
```

---

## 6. Results

```elixir
report =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.report(
    results,
    plan
  )

AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_report_markdown(
  report
)
```

### Prover comparison

```elixir
IO.puts("| Prover | Total | Solved | Failed | Solve Rate |")
IO.puts("|--------|------:|-------:|-------:|-----------:|")

Enum.each(report.by_prover, fn result ->
  IO.puts(
    "| #{result.prover} | " <>
      "#{result.total} | " <>
      "#{result.solved} | " <>
      "#{result.failed} | " <>
      "#{Float.round(result.solve_rate * 100, 1)}% |"
  )
end)
```

### Persist benchmark results

```elixir
paths =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.persist_run!(
    plan,
    results,
    report
  )

IO.puts("Run: #{paths.run_path}")
IO.puts("Results: #{paths.results_path}")
IO.puts("Report: #{paths.report_path}")
```
